WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.320
There's an interesting contrast of polling
data today.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:25.880
Donald Trump's approval rating is six points
lower than support for his impeachment.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.330
According to a new poll from Quinnipiac university.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:35.570
And according to this poll, Trump's approval
is 41% and support for his impeachment and

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:36.570
removal.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.170
This is not support for the inquiry.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:43.370
This is support for Trump's impeachment and
removal is at 47% support.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:48.989
This is definitely what you would call polling
underwater and also notable is that the same

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:55.780
poll from September 30th compared to this
poll five days earlier, saw a 30% increase

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.090
in the number that want to impeach and remove
Donald Trump.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:05.750
Five days prior support for impeachment and
removal was 37% five days later support goes

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:13.229
to 47% that's an increase of a 28 ish, somewhere
between 25 and 30% now it's important to understand

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:15.760
the historical context here.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.450
47% already believe that Donald Trump should
be removed from office.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:26.649
That's not the number of people that are saying
merely start the inquiry and if you contrast

00:01:26.649 --> 00:01:32.850
this to Nixon in the 70s impeachment support
for Nixon was I believe in the 20s when the

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.480
inquiry started, but very different circumstances.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:41.499
Nixon didn't have entire media outlets dedicated
to propping him up the way that Donald Trump

00:01:41.499 --> 00:01:42.740
has propping him up.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:48.740
And once again, it is now getting real enough
that the questions of wouldn't Pence be worse,

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:50.200
are starting to come up.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.460
And in many ways he would.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:58.969
An evangelical Christian supremacist like
Mike Pence would be much worse than Donald

00:01:58.969 --> 00:01:59.969
Trump in many ways.

00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:04.249
But I don't believe that that is a question
that is going to actually become a anything

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:05.249
more than theory.

00:02:05.249 --> 00:02:10.479
Because once again, you know, to either reset
or as a reminder, this impeachment inquiry

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:12.790
is not going to lead to the removal of Trump.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.730
I know every time I say this, a few people
email me, they say, here's how it could, here's

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:17.810
how it might.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.030
Uh, that's great.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:23.840
I don't think it's going to happen, but hopefully
it will damage Trump's reelection chances

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.750
such that he loses in 2020.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.480
We'll keep following the numbers as the process
moves forward.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.170
But I want to hear from you, what do you make
of these impeachment numbers?

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:37.390
What do you make of the historical context
around the impeachment support that there

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.441
now is not only for the inquiry but [inaudible]

00:02:39.441 --> 00:02:41.200
for the removal of Donald Trump.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.970
I'm on Twitter at the Pacman.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.100
The show is on Twitter at David Pakman show.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.170
I look forward to hearing from you there

